{title: 368 - Watchman, Blow the Gospel Trumpet}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #368 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 368}
{meta: category Christian Church - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Ab/Eb]Watchman, [Eb]blow the gospel [Cm]trumpet, [Ab]Every [Db/Ab]soul [Bbm]a warning [Fm]give;
[Gdim]Whosoever [Ab/Eb]hears [Eb]the message May repent, [Cm]and, turn and live.
[Ab/Eb]Blow the trumpet, [Gdim]trusty watchman, [Eb/G]Blow it loud o'er land and sea;
[Bbm]God commissions, [Eb/G]sound [Eb7]the mes [Fm/C]sage! [Ab]Every captive [Fm]may befree.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Cm/G]Blow the trumpet, [Fm/Ab]trusty [Cm/G]watchman,
[Ab]Blow it loud [Eb]o'er land [Ab]and sea;
[Ab]God commissions, sound the message!
[Ab]Every captive may be free.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Ab/Eb]Sound [Eb]it loud [Cm]o'r [Ab/Eb]every [Bbm]hilltop,
[Gdim]Gloomy [Eb]shade and sunny [Cm]plain;
[Ab/Eb]Ocean [Gdim]depths repeat [Eb/G]the message,
[Bbm]Full [Eb/G]salvation's [Ab]glad [Fm]refrain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Ab/Eb]Sound [Eb]it in [Cm]the [Ab]hedge [Db/Ab]and [Bbm]highway,
[Gdim]Earth's dark [Ab/Eb]spots [Eb]where exiles [Cm]roam;
[Ab/Eb]Let it [Gdim]tell all [Eb/G]things are ready,
[Bbm]Father [Eb7]waits [Fm/C]to [Ab]welcome [Fm]home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Ab/Eb]Sound [Eb]it for [Cm]the [Ab]heavy [Bbm]laden,
[Gdim]Weary, [Eb]longing to [Cm]be free;
[Ab/Eb]Sound a [Gdim]Savior's [Eb/G]invitation,
[Bbm]Sweetly [Eb7]saying, [Ab]"Come to [Fm]me."
{end_of_verse}
